Subject: Hide the panel Opacity group when the Plasma style has no adaptive transparency

PanelView reports a Translucent panel whenever the style turns adaptive
transparency off, and the configuration dialog shows that as a disabled
combo box whatever the style really draws, so an opaque style's panel
reads "Translucent". Without the option there is nothing to choose, so the
group is not shown.

diff -ruN a/desktoppackage/contents/configuration/PanelConfiguration.qml b/desktoppackage/contents/configuration/PanelConfiguration.qml
--- a/desktoppackage/contents/configuration/PanelConfiguration.qml
+++ b/desktoppackage/contents/configuration/PanelConfiguration.qml
@@ -450,6 +450,10 @@
         ColumnLayout {
             Layout.alignment: Qt.AlignHCenter
             spacing: Kirigami.Units.mediumSpacing
+            // A style without adaptive transparency draws its panel one way,
+            // and the panel reports Translucent whatever that way is: the
+            // group would only show a disabled choice that may be wrong.
+            visible: panel.adaptiveOpacityEnabled
             RowLayout {
                 Layout.alignment: Qt.AlignTop | Qt.AlignHCenter
                 spacing: 0
